  "content": "Death toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nThe death toll from landslides and floods triggered by continuous rainfall on Friday and Saturday has reached 52.\nAccording to the latest report from Nepal Police, a total of 52 people have lost their lives across the country.\nAmong them, the highest number of deaths has been reported in the districts of Koshi Province. In Ilam alone, 37 people have died, while Udayapur and Khotang each reported 2 deaths, and Panchthar reported 8 deaths.\nSimilarly, 3 people have died in Rautahat due to flooding.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nKathmandu\nLandslide\nnepali cricket\nflood\nrainfall\ndisaster\nnatural disaster\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nLong-distance travel from Kathmandu remains suspended, tickets to be refunded\n12 hours ago\n126 disaster-induced deaths in four months\n2 months ago\nNo shortage of funds for disaster management, says Minister Bishnu Poudel\n4 months ago\nStrengthening community ties through disaster preparedness and early action in Nepal\n12 months ago\nOver Rs 30 million collected in PM Disaster Relief Fund\n12 months ago\n228 die in recent natural disaster: Home Ministry\n1 year ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nAryatara chosen as new Kumari\nFire rages near Kasthamandap, largely under control\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n2 